WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
Here is our puzzle's ramp rule: no steeper
than a rise of one for every twelve

2
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.290
along.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.480
Ramp P rises nought point six metres
over nine metres along the ground.

4
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:17.000
Ramp Q is drawn on axes as the
line y equals nought point one x.

5
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.610
Ramp R rises nought point two
five metres over three metres.

6
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.170
Which ramps pass?

7
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.420
Only the longest?

8
00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:25.350
Two of them?

9
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.630
All three?

10
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.750
In this mission, you'll measure
steepness with gradient:

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.450
rise over run.

12
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.450
You'll see that one for every
twelve is a gradient of one twelfth,

13
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.360
and that a bigger gradient
means a steeper line.

14
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.170
And you'll read the gradient,
m, from y equals m x plus c.

15
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.680
Your mission: decide which
of the three ramps are legal.
